        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Igbo-Ukwu culture</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-ukwu">Igbo-Ukwu</a>, a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anambra-state">Anambra State</a>, south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, on a ridge between the Aghomili and Obizi rivers; sites <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> Isaiah (a shrine), Igbo Richard (a burial chamber) and Igbo Jonah (a cache)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">Dated to the 9th century CE by Thurstan Shaw’s radiocarbon dates (1970); newer dates from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/igbo-people">Igbo</a> Isaiah (2022) fall in the 10th–13th centuries, suggesting the sites were in use for several centuries</span></div>
